 ("galvanized pipe", "Steel pipe coated with zinc, used in older homes. It rusts from the inside, which narrows the pipe and lowers pressure.", "/services/repiping/"),
 ("ground microphone", "A sensitive listening tool set on soil or concrete to hear the sound of a leak below.", "/services/underground-leak-detection/"),
 ("HDPE", "High-density polyethylene, a tough, flexible plastic pipe often used for buried water service lines and pipe bursting.", "/blog/trenchless-water-line-replacement/"),
 ("hose bib", "An outdoor faucet. A dripping hose bib is an easy leak to miss.", "/blog/why-is-my-water-bill-so-high/"),
 ("hydrostatic test", "Filling a pipe system with water under pressure and watching for a pressure drop, which shows a leak.", "/services/sewer-line-repair/"),
 ("infrared camera", "A camera that shows temperature differences. A hot-water leak or wet area often shows up as a warm or cool spot.", "/services/slab-leak-repair/"),
 ("irrigation line", "The buried pipes that feed lawn sprinklers. A broken irrigation line can look like a service line leak.", "/services/underground-leak-detection/"),
 ("isolation test", "Shutting valves one at a time to narrow a leak down to one section of pipe.", "/services/underground-leak-detection/"),
 ("lateral", "The private sewer pipe that carries wastewater from a house to the public sewer main.", "/services/sewer-line-repair/"),
 ("lead service line", "A water service line made of lead. Federal rules require water systems to inventory service line materials and replace lead lines.", "/blog/who-is-responsible-for-water-line-from-street-to-house/"),
 ("leak adjustment", "A credit some utilities give on a high bill after a customer repairs a leak. Rules vary by utility.", "/blog/why-is-my-water-bill-so-high/"),
 ("line locating", "Tracing where a buried pipe runs, often with a transmitter and receiver, before digging.", "/services/underground-leak-detection/"),
 ("main shut-off valve", "The valve that turns off water to the whole house, usually where the service line enters or near the meter.", "/blog/how-to-shut-off-water-to-house/"),
 ("meter box", "The in-ground box near the street that holds the water meter and often the utility's valve.", "/blog/who-is-responsible-for-water-line-from-street-to-house/"),
 ("moisture meter", "A handheld tool that measures moisture in floors, walls or baseboards to map how far water has spread.", "/services/slab-leak-repair/"),
 ("Orangeburg pipe", "A sewer pipe made of tar-soaked wood fiber, used in some mid-1900s homes. It can soften, flatten and collapse.", "/services/sewer-line-repair/"),
 ("PEX", "Cross-linked polyethylene, a flexible plastic water pipe common in repipes and new homes.", "/services/repiping/"),
 ("pinhole leak", "A tiny hole in a pipe wall, most often in copper, that sprays or drips water.", "/blog/pinhole-leaks-copper-pipes/"),
 ("pipe bursting", "A trenchless method that pulls a new pipe through the old one, breaking the old pipe apart as it goes.", "/blog/trenchless-water-line-replacement/"),
